Retained: complete Llama/Mistral/Qwen2 causal-LM precompute stacks, runtime
forward functions, attention/recompute selectors, RoPE/masking and greedy
decode/vanilla functions. Qwen3 support is KVBench's integrated adaptation.
Excluded: datasets, chunking/evaluation/precompute CLI scripts, metrics, plots,
experiment configs, disk KV utilities, classification/QA heads, eviction
baselines, global monkeypatch entry points and the upstream environment freeze.

KVBench adaptations: private relative imports; local runtime classes instead
of global Transformers/Cache patches; Transformers 4.57 RoPE/head-dim
compatibility; native Qwen3 normed projections; inline Mistral/Qwen mask fixes;
shared checkpoint storage for precompute/runtime (including tied aliases); isolated JSONL workers using
the project Python; Hub/local checkpoint loading without checkout-relative
cache directories or a forced PyTorch .bin format.
Latency boundaries wait for offline CUDA precompute to finish and for the
first generated token to be ready before recording TTFT.

The upstream commit contains no repository-wide LICENSE. Original Apache-2.0
copyright/license headers in the precompute model files are retained;
LICENSE-APACHE-2.0 applies to those explicitly marked files. No license is
asserted for upstream files that carry no notice.
